    "description": "Iran’s foreign relations combine regional diplomacy, nuclear negotiations, economic relationships, and cooperation with major powers. Understanding them requires separating diplomatic declarations, institutional authority, and documented outcomes, especially where sanctions and security disputes intersect.",
